Hi,

On an Intel BE201 (8086:a876) the controller stops accepting HCI
commands at runtime. A few minutes later the firmware raises a
hardware exception and the driver never recovers. hci0 stays
registered, but every command fails with -19 until the PCI driver is
unbound and rebound by hand. Rebinding brings it back.

It has happened on two consecutive days with the same signature:

  - 2026-10-06: about 6 minutes after a cold boot, with no suspend or
    hibernate in that boot.
  - 2026-10-05: about 12 minutes after an s2idle resume.

So this does not look like the resume problems addressed by the
recent "btintel_pcie: two PM fixes" series.

System
------
  Machine:   Lenovo ThinkPad X1 Carbon Gen 13 (21NS005RUS), BIOS N4BET69W (1.39)
  SoC:       Intel Lunar Lake
  BT:        Intel BE201, 00:14.7 [8086:a876] rev 10, subsys [8086:000e]
  Firmware:  intel/ibt-0190-0291-pci.sfi, Firmware Version 141-26.26,
             timestamp 2026.26 buildtype 1 build 125325, SHA1 0xfa98b015
             Bootloader timestamp 2023.33 buildtype 1 build 45995
  Kernel:    7.2.9-1-cachyos (distro kernel, CachyOS / Arch)
  linux-firmware: 20260916
  BlueZ:     5.87

Usage at the time: AirPods Pro streaming A2DP, plus an LE keyboard
connected. On 10-06 a Steam game was starting at the moment of the
exception. I don't know whether that is related.

Sequence (2026-10-06, monotonic timestamps)
-------------------------------------------
1) Stage 1, t=355s: MAC access fails, then every command times out.
   The two commands below then repeat about every 11 s for roughly
   10 minutes (58x each). Opcode 0x2005 is LE Set Random Address and
   0x2041 is LE Set Extended Scan Parameters.

  [  355.470040] Bluetooth: hci0: Failed to get mac access -62
  [  355.470245] Bluetooth: hci0: failed to log fwtrigger event
  [  355.489016] Bluetooth: hci0: Failed to get mac access: (-62)
  [  356.436142] Bluetooth: hci0: Timeout (500 ms) on tx completion
  [  356.436336] Bluetooth: hci0: Failed to send frame (-62)
  [  356.436369] Bluetooth: hci0: sending frame failed (-62)
  [  356.436391] Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x2005 failed: -62
  [  356.940130] Bluetooth: hci0: Timeout (500 ms) on tx completion
  [  356.940250] Bluetooth: hci0: Failed to send frame (-62)
  [  356.940298] Bluetooth: hci0: sending frame failed (-62)
  [  356.940319] Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x2041 failed: -62

   At t~967s the A2DP stream fails. bluetoothd logs "avdtp.c:
   cancel_request() Start: Connection timed out (110)".

2) Stage 2, t=998s: hardware exception, controller in error state.

  [  998.173094] Bluetooth: hci0: Received hw exception interrupt
  [  998.173266] Bluetooth: hci0: Received gp1 mailbox interrupt
  [  998.173284] Bluetooth: hci0: Controller device warning
(boot_stage: 0xe0fb1047)
  [  998.176122] Bluetooth: hci0: Received gp1 mailbox interrupt
  [  998.176159] Bluetooth: hci0: Controller device warning
(boot_stage: 0xd0fb7047)
  [  998.176173] Bluetooth: hci0: Controller device warning
(boot_stage: 0xd0fb7047)
  [  998.176183] Bluetooth: hci0: Controller in error state
(boot_stage: 0xd0fb7047)
  [  998.176191] Bluetooth: hci0: Controller device warning
(boot_stage: 0xd0fb7047)
  [  998.176201] Bluetooth: hci0: Invalid exception dump signature: 0xb41054f9

3) Stage 3: no FLR or recovery is attempted. Everything after this
   fails with -ENODEV.

  [ 1019.202019] Bluetooth: hci0: sending frame failed (-19)
  [ 1019.202087] Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x2039 failed: -19
  [ 1063.238257] Bluetooth: hci0: Opcode 0x2005 failed: -19
  ...

   From userspace: "bluetoothctl power off" fails with
   org.bluez.Error.Failed, and connect returns "InProgress
   br-connection-busy".

4) Recovery. Unbind and rebind recover fully: firmware reloads and
   devices reconnect.

  echo 0000:00:14.7 > /sys/bus/pci/drivers/btintel_pcie/unbind
  echo 0000:00:14.7 > /sys/bus/pci/drivers/btintel_pcie/bind

The 2026-10-05 occurrence is the same: s2idle exit at 1828s, the first
"Failed to get mac access -62" at 2536s, then "Received hw exception
interrupt" at 2846s with the same boot_stage values (0xe0fb1047 ->
0xd0fb7047) and "Invalid exception dump signature: 0xb63354f9", then
-19 forever.

Attached are the full Bluetooth-related kernel logs for both boots:
  dmesg-2026-10-06.txt
  dmesg-2026-10-05.txt

Questions
---------
- After "Controller in error state" the driver does not seem to
  schedule a reset/FLR, and hci0 is left in a state where every send
  returns -ENODEV. Is recovery expected to happen here? Is this
  related to the pending "btintel_pcie: serialize ... reset" work?
- Is the initial "Failed to get mac access -62" at runtime a known
  firmware issue on BE201 with build 125325, and is a newer firmware
  available?
- "Invalid exception dump signature" means no exception data was
  captured. Is there anything I should collect on the next occurrence
  before rebinding, such as writing to the devcoredump "coredump"
  attribute or a btmon trace?

I'm happy to test patches, or to try reproducing on bluetooth-next if
that helps. It happens about once a day here.

Thanks,
kstgrd

